data.content:
Here are the **three EF Core 10 breaking changes** affecting your code and how to fix each:

---

## 1. `ExecuteUpdateAsync` — Now accepts a regular lambda

Expression tree construction no longer compiles. Replace with a simple lambda:

```csharp
// .NET 10 fix
await context.Blogs.ExecuteUpdateAsync(s =>
{
    s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, 8);
    if (nameChanged)
    {
        s.SetProperty(b => b.Name, "foo");
    }
});
```

No more `Expression.Lambda`/`Expression.Call` gymnastics needed.

---

## 2. Complex type column names are now uniquified/use full path

Two changes hit you:
- **Duplicate property names** (e.g., `Street` on both `ShippingAddress` and `BillingAddress`) get a numeric suffix appended.
- **Nested complex types** now use the full path: `Order.Payment.BillingAddress.City` maps to `Payment_BillingAddress_City` (was `BillingAddress_City`).

Both generate rename migrations. **Fix:** pin column names explicitly:

```csharp
b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress, ab =>
{
    ab.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("ShippingAddress_Street");
});
b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress, ab =>
{
    ab.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("BillingAddress_Street");
});

// For nested:
b.ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment, pb =>
{
    pb.ComplexProperty(p => p.BillingAddress, ba =>
    {
        ba.Property(a => a.City).HasColumnName("BillingAddress_City");
    });
});
```

---

## 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — new `logCommandText` parameter

All methods like `CommandReaderExecuting` now require an additional `string logCommandText` parameter:

```csharp
public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
    IRelationalConnection connection, DbCommand command,
    DbContext context, Guid commandId, Guid connectionId,
    DateTimeOffset startTime,
    string logCommandText)   // ← add this
{
    // logCommandText contains redacted SQL safe for logging
    // command.CommandText has the actual SQL
}
```

Update all method signatures in your `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` implementation accordingly (`CommandReaderExecuted`, `CommandScalarExecuting`, etc. all have the same addition).
